==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|houwan|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|hawwanan|lang=gem-pro}}. Cognate with English {{term|hew}}.

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=7|haut|[[haute]]''' ''or archaic'' '''[[hieb]]|[[gehauen]]''' ''or colloquial'' '''[[gehaut]]}}

# {{transitive|colloquial|lang=de}} to [[beat]]; to [[hit]] (someone); to [[spank]]
#: ''Ich '''hau''' dich gleich.'' — “Now I’m going to spank you.”
# {{reflexive|colloquial|of multiple people|lang=de}} to [[fight]]; to [[tangle]]
# {{transitive}} to [[chop]]; to chop down; to [[cut]]; to [[whittle]]; to [[hew]]

====Conjugation====
In casual speech, {{term|hauen}} is often conjugated like a weak verb, with the past tense {{term|haute}}, etc.

'''Weak Conjugation'''
{{de-conj-weak|hau|gehauen|h}}
'''Strong Conjugation (archaic)'''
{{de-conj-strong|hau|hieb|gehauen|h|||hieb|a}}

